# Jennifer is not a GitHub Linguist language yet. An override naming a language
# Linguist does not know is not a label but an exclusion: the .j files drop out
# of the statistics, and the language bar is left to whatever else is in the
# repository. Without the override they are guessed as JASS / Objective-J
# instead.
#
# So nothing else is counted either, and the bar stays empty until Linguist
# learns Jennifer. The Jennifer lines are already right for that day:
# the sources, and the launchers, which carry a jennifer shebang and no
# extension.
* linguist-detectable=false
*.j linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
bin/deckadmin linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
bin/healthcheck linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
bin/serve linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
